{"calibration_results":[{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:complete-frame-mismatch","evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","invented_material_premise":false,"rationale":"The registered target covers all 100 planned locations, but the only selected result uses the 73 screened-in locations as its denominator and reports that conditional value as the planned-region rate, with no amendment or approved deviation. This directly demonstrates a target-denominator mismatch. Falsification attempt: an approved scope change or a claim limited to retained locations could defeat the issue, but the vignette expressly states neither applies.","verdict":"demonstrated_issue"},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:conditional-subset-scope","evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","invented_material_premise":false,"rationale":"The registered target, selected denominator, and reported claim all concern exactly the 73 signal-eligible locations. Falsification attempt: a claim about all planned locations would create a mismatch, but the vignette states every claim is limited to signal-eligible locations.","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope"},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:full-frame-accounting","evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","invented_material_premise":false,"rationale":"The target covers all 100 planned locations, and the selected result retains all 100 in the denominator while recording the 27 unavailable measurements and reporting the full-frame rate. Falsification attempt: exclusion of the unavailable locations from the denominator would show a frame mismatch, but the vignette expressly states they remain included.","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope"},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:unrelated-quality-endpoint","evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","invented_material_premise":false,"rationale":"The selected scientific result uses all 100 planned locations. The 73-record fraction belongs to a separate quality-control table explicitly excluded from the scientific endpoint, so it does not demonstrate a denominator issue in that endpoint. Falsification attempt: use of the quality-control fraction as the scientific result would matter, but the vignette expressly excludes that relationship.","verdict":"no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope"},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:conflicting-scope-records","evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","invented_material_premise":false,"rationale":"Equally authoritative signed plans specify conflicting target populations, neither has precedence, and the selected eligible-location result conforms to one but not the other. Falsification attempt: precedence between the plans would resolve whether the selected scope is valid, but the vignette states no precedence exists; the governing scope therefore remains materially unknown.","verdict":"conditional_or_unknown"},{"calibration_case_id":"calibration:no-selected-result","evidence_basis":"stated_evidence_only","invented_material_premise":false,"rationale":"The workflow can emit multiple runtime-selected reports, but the preserved record does not establish which report, if any, supported the scientific claim. Falsification attempt: a preserved runtime selection or claim-to-report linkage could permit evaluation, but neither is stated, leaving insufficient evidence to assess a specific selected result.","verdict":"insufficient_evidence"}],"reviewer_participant_id":"actor:stage1-recovery-codex-03"}